# Known bugs of the guide scripts, found by tools/check-container-image and waiting for Phase 1.
# Columns, separated by a tab:
#   id | pattern | what is wrong | OS majors (optional: "10" or "8,9"; empty means all) | package the image needs (optional)
# The pattern is an awk regular expression, matched against a leftover line such as
# "M /etc/fstab", "unit crond.service enabled" or "cmdline missing console=tty0". A dash means
# that the check finds the bug in code. A bug that is observed and not listed fails the run.
# So does a listed bug that is no longer observed on an image it applies to: delete its line in the
# change that fixes it.
runtime-unit-left-enabled	lowlat-runtime\.service	apply-all has no --rollback: lowlat-runtime.service stays installed and enabled
